---
const pageTitle = 'vitrify — production record for ceramic ateliers';
const pageDescription =
  'vitrify is a professional production record for ceramic ateliers: physical pieces, firing history, kiln planning, stock state, and atelier memory.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="page">
      <header class="topbar">
        <a class="brand" href="/vitrify/" aria-label="vitrify home">
          <span>vitrify</span>
          <em>by res factae</em>
        </a>

        <nav class="nav" aria-label="Page navigation">
          <a href="#record">Record</a>
          <a href="#kiln">Kiln</a>
          <a href="#stock">Stock</a>
          <a href="#memory">Memory</a>
        </nav>

        <a class="top-cta" href="#access">Request access</a>
      </header>

      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="label">For ceramic and porcelain ateliers</p>
          <h1>The production record for ceramic ateliers.</h1>
          <p class="intro">
            Track physical pieces, firing history, kiln planning, stock state, and atelier memory —
            from making to ready work.
          </p>

          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="#record">See what it records</a>
            <a class="button secondary" href="#access">Request access</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="studio-panel" aria-label="Example vitrify studio overview">
          <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
              <span>Atelier record</span>
              <strong>Today</strong>
            </div>
            <em>example</em>
          </div>

          <div class="record-stack">
            <article>
              <span>physical pieces</span>
              <strong>184</strong>
              <p>registered across stock, clients, classes, and experiments</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>next firing</span>
              <strong>74%</strong>
              <p>estimated kiln load from waiting pieces</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>ready stock</span>
              <strong>76</strong>
              <p>finished work currently available or assigned</p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="panel-note">
            <span>recent firing</span>
            <strong>glaze · 18 pieces · 2 losses recorded</strong>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="problem">
        <p>
          Ceramic production rarely lives in one place.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some of it is on shelves, some in kiln notes, some in messages, some in memory,
          some in shop stock, and some nowhere at all.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="record" class="section spine-section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="label">Production spine</p>
          <h2>Built around the physical piece.</h2>
          <p>
            vitrify starts with the object itself: what exists, where it is in production,
            what happened to it, and what the atelier can trust later.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="spine">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Piece</h3>
            <p>One record for one physical object, not a vague quantity counter.</p>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>State</h3>
            <p>Clear production state without forcing every studio into one technique.</p>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Firing</h3>
            <p>History of kiln events, included pieces, timing, and outcomes.</p>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>04</span>
            <h3>History</h3>
            <p>A usable atelier memory for stock, losses, decisions, and future production.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="kiln" class="section kiln-section">
        <div class="kiln-copy">
          <p class="label">Kiln planning</p>
          <h2>Plan firings without turning vitrify into a kiln controller.</h2>
          <p>
            Estimate load, see what is waiting, record firing history, and understand when
            work should become available again.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="schedule" aria-label="Example kiln planning board">
          <article>
            <span>waiting</span>
            <strong>42 pieces</strong>
            <p>ready to be included in a future firing</p>
          </article>

          <article class="active">
            <span>next load</span>
            <strong>74% estimate</strong>
            <p>capacity based on studio size categories</p>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>available</span>
            <strong>Tue 09:30</strong>
            <p>from firing and cooling assumptions</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="stock" class="section stock-section">
        <div class="section-head">
          <p class="label">Stock state</p>
          <h2>Know what is ready, missing, or still in progress.</h2>
          <p>
            Sales tools begin when something can be sold. vitrify begins earlier:
            while the work is still moving through the atelier.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="stock-grid">
          <article>
            <span>Ready</span>
            <strong>finished work</strong>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>Missing</span>
            <strong>stock gaps</strong>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>Assigned</span>
            <strong>clients, classes, fairs</strong>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>In progress</span>
            <strong>work before inventory</strong>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="memory" class="section memory-section">
        <div class="memory-card">
          <p class="label">Atelier memory</p>
          <h2>Statistics should come from good records, not extra admin.</h2>
          <p>
            Over time, vitrify can show useful atelier patterns: recurring losses,
            forms that sell, stock gaps, firing outcomes, and what should be produced again.
          </p>
          <p>
            These statistics are not a separate workflow. They are a result of recording
            pieces, firings, stock movement, and outcomes in one structured place.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="insight-list" aria-label="Example future statistics">
          <article>
            <span>recurring loss</span>
            <strong>large platter</strong>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>stock gap</span>
            <strong>small bowl</strong>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>best movement</span>
            <strong>matte green cup</strong>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section commerce-section">
        <div class="commerce-copy">
          <p class="label">Production before sales</p>
          <h2>Shopify and vitrify are not the same job.</h2>
          <p>
            Shopify manages the storefront. vitrify manages the production side:
            pieces, batches, firings, stock state, losses, planning, and atelier history.
          </p>
          <p>
            Later, vitrify can support stock updates or synchronization with Shopify,
            while keeping the production record inside the atelier.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="read-more">
        <details>
          <summary>Technique flexibility</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              vitrify should not belong to one ceramic method. It should support studios
              working with wheel throwing, hand-building, slab work, casting, sculpture,
              tiles, tableware, teaching stock, and production batches.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What vitrify is not</summary>
          <div>
            <p>
              vitrify is not booking, invoicing, CRM, a public storefront, a kiln controller,
              or a ceramic encyclopedia. It is focused on the production record.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section id="access" class="access">
        <p class="label">Early development</p>
        <h2>Shape vitrify with real atelier production.</h2>
        <p>
          The first version is being designed for ceramic and porcelain ateliers that need
          clearer production, firing, stock, loss, and history tracking.
        </p>

        <!-- TODO: confirm real contact email before public launch. -->
        <a class="button primary" href="mailto:hello@resfactae.xyz?subject=vitrify%20early%20access">
          Request access
        </a>
      </section>

      <footer class="footer">
        <span>vitrify by res factae</span>
        <nav>
          <a href="/">res factae</a>
          <a href="/work/vitrify/">project note</a>
        </nav>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: "Apfel Grotezk";
    src: url("/fonts/apfel/ApfelGrotezk-Regular.woff2") format("woff2");
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: "Apfel Grotezk";
    src: url("/fonts/apfel/ApfelGrotezk-Mittel.woff2") format("woff2");
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: "Apfel Grotezk";
    src: url("/fonts/apfel/ApfelGrotezk-Fett.woff2") format("woff2");
    font-weight: 750;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    --ink: #111827;
    --muted: #5b6472;
    --quiet: #7a8392;
    --line: rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.14);
    --line-strong: rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.24);

    --page: #f7f9fd;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --surface-blue: #eef5ff;
    --surface-cyan: #e8f8fb;
    --surface-green: #ecf8f1;
    --surface-violet: #f2efff;
    --surface-yellow: #fbf5d6;

    --blue: #7da8ff;
    --cyan: #6bd2e2;
    --green: #7fd7a4;
    --violet: #b8a4f4;
    --yellow: #ead45f;

    --radius: 18px;
    --radius-small: 10px;
    --max: 1160px;

    font-family:
      "Apfel Grotezk",
      "Afacad Flux",
      "Gill Sans",
      "Trebuchet MS",
      system-ui,
      sans-serif;
  }

  *,
  *::before,
  *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  html {
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    color: var(--ink);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 88% 4%, rgba(184, 164, 244, 0.2), transparent 34rem),
      radial-gradient(circle at 8% 18%, rgba(107, 210, 226, 0.16), transparent 30rem),
      linear-gradient(135deg, #fbfcff 0%, #f5f8fd 48%, #f8f9fc 100%);
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  p,
  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  strong,
  span,
  em,
  summary,
  a {
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .page {
    overflow-x: clip;
    min-height: 100vh;
  }

  .topbar,
  .hero,
  .problem,
  .section,
  .read-more,
  .access,
  .footer {
    width: min(var(--max), calc(100% - 32px));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .topbar {
    padding: 22px 0 12px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .brand {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: max-content;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .brand span {
    font-size: 1.48rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
  }

  .brand em {
    margin-top: 4px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-style: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .nav {
    justify-self: center;
    display: flex;
    gap: 4px;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 5px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
  }

  .nav a {
    padding: 8px 11px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .nav a:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--surface-blue);
  }

  .top-cta {
    min-height: 40px;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-small);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .top-cta:hover {
    background: var(--surface-cyan);
  }

  .hero {
    min-height: calc(100svh - 76px);
    padding: clamp(54px, 8vw, 96px) 0 clamp(48px, 7vw, 76px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(340px, 0.95fr);
    gap: clamp(34px, 6vw, 72px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .label {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: #3454c7;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3,
  p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 8.2vw, 7.6rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.058em;
    font-weight: 750;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    font-size: clamp(2.55rem, 4.9vw, 5.1rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.052em;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  h3 {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-size: 1.32rem;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: #283246;
    font-size: clamp(1.22rem, 2vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.24;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    margin-top: 30px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 46px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 12px 17px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-small);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .button.primary {
    color: white;
    background: var(--ink);
    border-color: var(--ink);
  }

  .button.primary:hover {
    background: #050914;
  }

  .button.secondary {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86);
  }

  .button.secondary:hover {
    background: var(--surface-blue);
  }

  .studio-panel {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 24px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 24px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    box-shadow: 0 28px 90px rgba(34, 55, 103, 0.1);
  }

  .panel-header {
    padding-bottom: 18px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .panel-header span,
  .panel-header em,
  .record-stack span,
  .panel-note span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .panel-header strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-size: 1.48rem;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .panel-header em {
    padding: 6px 9px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-blue);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .record-stack {
    margin-top: 16px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .record-stack article {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .record-stack article:nth-child(1) {
    background: var(--surface-blue);
  }

  .record-stack article:nth-child(2) {
    background: var(--surface-cyan);
  }

  .record-stack article:nth-child(3) {
    background: var(--surface-green);
  }

  .record-stack strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5.5vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .record-stack p {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    color: #313b4f;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .panel-note {
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding: 15px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface-violet);
  }

  .panel-note strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 5px;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .problem {
    padding: 0 0 clamp(58px, 8vw, 92px);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .problem p {
    min-height: 150px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 26px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
    font-size: clamp(1.28rem, 2.5vw, 2.16rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .problem p:nth-child(2) {
    background: var(--surface-violet);
  }

  .section,
  .read-more,
  .access {
    padding: clamp(62px, 9vw, 102px) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .section-head {
    max-width: 810px;
    margin-bottom: 34px;
  }

  .section-head p:not(.label),
  .kiln-copy p:not(.label),
  .memory-card p,
  .commerce-copy p,
  .access p {
    color: #283246;
    font-size: clamp(1.06rem, 1.45vw, 1.22rem);
  }

  .spine {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 24px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .spine article {
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: 250px;
    padding: 22px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .spine article + article {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .spine article:nth-child(1) {
    background: var(--surface-blue);
  }

  .spine article:nth-child(2) {
    background: var(--surface-cyan);
  }

  .spine article:nth-child(3) {
    background: var(--surface-green);
  }

  .spine article:nth-child(4) {
    background: var(--surface-violet);
  }

  .spine span {
    color: var(--quiet);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .spine h3 {
    margin-top: auto;
  }

  .spine p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: #313b4f;
  }

  .kiln-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.95fr) minmax(360px, 1.05fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 66px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .schedule {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .schedule article {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .schedule article.active {
    background: var(--surface-cyan);
  }

  .schedule span,
  .stock-grid span,
  .insight-list span {
    display: block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .schedule strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 7px;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .schedule p {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    color: #313b4f;
  }

  .stock-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .stock-grid article {
    min-height: 160px;
    padding: 18px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .stock-grid article:nth-child(1) {
    background: var(--surface-green);
  }

  .stock-grid article:nth-child(2) {
    background: var(--surface-yellow);
  }

  .stock-grid article:nth-child(3) {
    background: var(--surface-blue);
  }

  .stock-grid article:nth-child(4) {
    background: var(--surface-violet);
  }

  .stock-grid strong {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .memory-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(320px, 0.9fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 58px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .memory-card {
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 44px);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 24px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .insight-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .insight-list article {
    padding: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .insight-list article:nth-child(1) {
    background: var(--surface-violet);
  }

  .insight-list article:nth-child(2) {
    background: var(--surface-yellow);
  }

  .insight-list article:nth-child(3) {
    background: var(--surface-green);
  }

  .insight-list strong {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 1.34rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .commerce-copy {
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .commerce-section {
    background:
      linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, transparent),
      transparent;
  }

  .commerce-copy h2 {
    max-width: 880px;
  }

  .commerce-copy p {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .read-more {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  details {
